import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.EnlargedEtaleRingedSite

/-! # The invariant-spectrum quotient of a free split-torus action

Source: Cesnavicius, Problems about torsors over regular rings, arXiv:2201.06424v4,
Sections 1.2.3 and 1.3.1; Stacks Project, Tags 0EKK and 00WH
(blueprint: lem-sfb-affine-free-split-torus-invariants).

The split torus is Spec of the group algebra of Z^r, with its canonical Hopf group law.
The invariant ring and its inclusion map reuse the affine-relation constructions.
The isomorphism remembers the canonical quotient morphism after sheafification.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.MonoidalCategory Opposite
open scoped TensorProduct CategoryTheory.MonObj

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- The action map in affine tensor coordinates, using the canonical affine
fibre-product isomorphism. Its contravariant ring map is the coaction rho.
Source: Stacks Project, Tags 01I4 and 0EKK
(blueprint: lem-sfb-affine-free-split-torus-invariants). -/
def affineSplitTorusActionCoordinates
    (R A : Type u) [CommRing R] [CommRing A] [Algebra R A] (r : ℕ)
    [ModObj ((Spec (.of (AddMonoidAlgebra R (Fin r → ℤ)))).asOver (Spec (.of R)))
      ((Spec (.of A)).asOver (Spec (.of R)))] :
    Spec (.of (AddMonoidAlgebra R (Fin r → ℤ) ⊗[R] A)) ⟶ Spec (.of A) :=
  (pullbackSpecIso R (AddMonoidAlgebra R (Fin r → ℤ)) A).inv ≫
    (ModObj.smul
      (M := (Spec (.of (AddMonoidAlgebra R (Fin r → ℤ)))).asOver (Spec (.of R)))
      (X := (Spec (.of A)).asOver (Spec (.of R)))).left

/-- A free split-torus action on an affine finite-type scheme over a Noetherian
ring has fppf quotient the spectrum of its invariant subring, with quotient map
induced by inclusion. The coequalizer of action and projection is the pointwise
orbit presheaf. The equation with its projection identifies the quotient morphism.
The representable presheaf is lifted only to accommodate sheafification's universe.

Source: Cesnavicius, arXiv:2201.06424v4, Sections 1.2.3 and 1.3.1;
Stacks Project, Tags 0EKK, 07S1 and 00WH
(blueprint: lem-sfb-affine-free-split-torus-invariants).

Proof plan:
1. Expand the coaction in Laurent monomials. Counit and coassociativity give a
   direct Z^r-grading, and multiplicativity makes it a ring grading (Tag 0EKK).
   The equalizer defining affineRelationInvariants is exactly A_0.
2. In A[Z^r] let I be generated by a(t^m-1) for homogeneous a of degree m,
   and J by t^m-1. The universal stabilizer algebra A[Z^r]/I gives a fixed
   test point. Freeness on that test scheme forces t_i=1, hence I=J.
   Uses: def-weil-affine-spectrum, def-weil-pbc-algebra-hom-quotient.
3. Apply lem-sfb-graded-stabilizer-strong-products to get finite expressions
   1=sum_j a_ij b_ij in each pair of opposite standard-basis degrees.
4. Products f of one a_ij b_ij for each i give a principal-open cover of
   Spec A_0. Localizing at f makes the chosen a_ij homogeneous units.
   The direct grading survives localization and its degree-zero ring is A_0[1/f].
   Rank zero uses the single empty product f=1.
   Uses: lem-weil-pbc-spec-basic-opens-unit-ideal-quasi-compact,
   def-weil-ring-localization-away, lem-weil-pbc-principal-localization-open-immersion.
5. The Laurent map z_i to the chosen homogeneous units is an equivariant
   isomorphism, with inverse c_m to (c_m u^(-m))z^m. Taking spectra gives
   local trivializations of the quotient and Zariski local sections.
   Uses: lem-weil-pbc-fibre-product-affine-spectra.
6. For any fppf sheaf, an invariant map from X descends by those local
   sections. On overlaps the sections differ by a torus point, so their images
   agree; sheaf gluing gives existence and the local sections give uniqueness.
   Thus the invariant spectrum represents sheafification of the orbit presheaf.
   Its map from X is Spec of the inclusion, and its S-structure is the descended
   structure map. Both source and base are affine, giving affineness over S.
   Uses: def-trf-scheme-algebraic-space, def-pc-fppf-site,
   def-weil-pbc-sheafification. -/
theorem affine_free_splitTorus_invariants
    (R A : Type u) [CommRing R] [CommRing A] [Algebra R A]
    [IsNoetherianRing R] [Algebra.FiniteType R A] (r : ℕ)
    [ModObj ((Spec (.of (AddMonoidAlgebra R (Fin r → ℤ)))).asOver (Spec (.of R)))
      ((Spec (.of A)).asOver (Spec (.of R)))]
    (hfree : ∀ (V : Over (Spec (.of R)))
      (t : V ⟶ (Spec (.of (AddMonoidAlgebra R (Fin r → ℤ)))).asOver (Spec (.of R)))
      (x : V ⟶ (Spec (.of A)).asOver (Spec (.of R))), t • x = x → t = 1) :
    ∃ m : Spec (.of (affineRelationInvariants (affineSplitTorusActionCoordinates R A r)
        (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
          (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight :
            A →ₐ[R] AddMonoidAlgebra R (Fin r → ℤ) ⊗[R] A))))) ⟶ Spec (.of R),
      ∃ hq : affineRelationQuotientMap (affineSplitTorusActionCoordinates R A r)
          (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
            (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight :
              A →ₐ[R] AddMonoidAlgebra R (Fin r → ℤ) ⊗[R] A))) ≫ m =
            Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap R A)),
        ∃ e : sheafify (Scheme.fppfTopology.over (Spec (.of R)))
            (coequalizer
              (yoneda.map (ModObj.smul
                (M := (Spec (.of (AddMonoidAlgebra R (Fin r → ℤ)))).asOver (Spec (.of R)))
                (X := (Spec (.of A)).asOver (Spec (.of R)))))
              (yoneda.map (CartesianMonoidalCategory.snd
                ((Spec (.of (AddMonoidAlgebra R (Fin r → ℤ)))).asOver (Spec (.of R)))
                ((Spec (.of A)).asOver (Spec (.of R))))) ⋙ uliftFunctor.{u + 1, u}) ≅
            yoneda.obj (Over.mk m) ⋙ uliftFunctor.{u + 1, u},
          Functor.whiskerRight (coequalizer.π
              (yoneda.map (ModObj.smul
                (M := (Spec (.of (AddMonoidAlgebra R (Fin r → ℤ)))).asOver (Spec (.of R)))
                (X := (Spec (.of A)).asOver (Spec (.of R)))))
              (yoneda.map (CartesianMonoidalCategory.snd
                ((Spec (.of (AddMonoidAlgebra R (Fin r → ℤ)))).asOver (Spec (.of R)))
                ((Spec (.of A)).asOver (Spec (.of R)))))) uliftFunctor.{u + 1, u} ≫
            toSheafify (Scheme.fppfTopology.over (Spec (.of R))) _ ≫ e.hom =
          Functor.whiskerRight (yoneda.map (Over.homMk
            (affineRelationQuotientMap (affineSplitTorusActionCoordinates R A r)
              (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
                (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight :
                  A →ₐ[R] AddMonoidAlgebra R (Fin r → ℤ) ⊗[R] A)))) hq))
            uliftFunctor.{u + 1, u} := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
